ing oral anticoagulant therapy. <source>Clin Chem</source><year>1995</year>;<volume>41</volume>:<fpage>1171</fpage>-6.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7628093</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">MacLaughlin EJ, Raehl CL, Treadway AK, Sterling TL, Zoller DP, Bond CA. Assessing medication adherence in the elderly: which tools to use in clinical practice? <source>Drugs Aging</source><year>2005</year>;<volume>22</volume>:<fpage>231</fpage>-55.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15813656</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><notes notes-type="citation-text"><p>Cite this as: <italic>BMJ</italic> 2009;338:b1492</p></notes></back></article>